 s told today (#): what\, to whom\n2. Lies caught before I spoke (#)\n3. Co
 rrections made (#)\n4. The trigger: who\, where\, how tired I was\, and th
 e fear (failure / rejection / conflict / looking weak)\n5. The story in my
  head: "If I tell the truth\, ___ will happen."\n6. What actually happened
  when I told the truth\n7. Tomorrow's risk moment\, written as an if-then:
