DESCRIPTION:Tonight's question: Who is it hardest to tell the truth to? Wh
 at do you fear they'll think of you?\n\nTHE LEDGER (10 min)\n1. Lies told 
 today (#): what\, to whom\n2. Lies caught before I spoke (#)\n3. Correctio
 ns made (#)\n4. The trigger: who\, where\, how tired I was\, and the fear 
 (failure / rejection / conflict / looking weak)\n5. The story in my head: 
 "If I tell the truth\, ___ will happen."\n6. What actually happened when I
  told the truth\n7. Tomorrow's risk moment\, written as an if-then: "If __
