DTSTART:20261102T063000
DTEND:20261102T063500
SUMMARY:Day 5 Morning: The alarm in your body
DESCRIPTION:Week 1: See It. You can't fix what you won't count.\n\nNotice 
 what your body does right before a lie: tight chest\, hot face\, dry throa
 t\, talking faster. That feeling is your alarm. Learn it today.\n\nBefore 
 you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nW
 hy it works: Break an automatic habit: notice it\, then replace it. Day 5 
 teaches you your body's alarm. The pause and a prepared true sentence (Wee
 k 4) are the replacement response. (Bate\, Malouff\, Thorsteinsson & Bhull
 ar (2011)\, Clinical Psychology Review (meta-analysis))
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 5 Morning: The alarm in your body
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
