SUMMARY:Day 10 Morning: Where it started
DESCRIPTION:Week 2: The Fear Underneath. Every lie is protecting something
 .\n\nAt some point today\, think back to the first time you remember lying
  to stay safe. Who were you protecting yourself from?\n\nBefore you go\, w
 rite today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it work
 s: Writing about hard things helps a little. The evening questions and let
 ters are writing exercises. They help\, but they're one tool among several
 \, not a cure. (Frattaroli (2006)\, Psychological Bulletin)
