SUMMARY:Day 11 Morning: Shame vs. guilt
DESCRIPTION:Week 2: The Fear Underneath. Every lie is protecting something
 .\n\nGuilt says "I did something wrong." Shame says "I am wrong." Shame dr
 ives lies. Catch shame talk in your head today and write it down.\n\nBefor
 e you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\
 nWhy it works: Shame hides. Guilt repairs. Day 11 teaches you to turn sham
 e sentences into guilt sentences. You can repair something you did. You ca
 n't repair who you are. (Tangney & Dearing\, Shame and Guilt (2002) and la
 ter reviews)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 11 Morning: Shame vs. guilt
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
