DESCRIPTION:Tonight's question: Rewrite one shame sentence as a guilt sent
 ence: "I did ___\, and I can make it right by ___."\n\nTHE LEDGER (10 min)
 \n1. Lies told today (#): what\, to whom\n2. Lies caught before I spoke (#
 )\n3. Corrections made (#)\n4. The trigger: who\, where\, how tired I was\
 , and the fear (failure / rejection / conflict / looking weak)\n5. The sto
 ry in my head: "If I tell the truth\, ___ will happen."\n6. What actually 
 happened when I told the truth\n7. Tomorrow's risk moment\, written as an 
 if-then: "If ___\, then I'll say ___."\n8. One line of prayer or thanks
