SUMMARY:Day 13 Morning: Test your prediction
DESCRIPTION:Week 2: The Fear Underneath. Every lie is protecting something
 .\n\nRun an experiment. Before one true thing you'd normally lie about tod
 ay\, write your prediction first: "If I say it\, ___ will happen." Then sa
 y it.\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'l
 l say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Lies are safety behaviors. Dropping them teac
 hes you that the truth is survivable. Each lie you don't tell is a test of
  your prediction. The prediction test (Day 13) and the truth ladder (Week 
 5) are behavioral experiments. (Clark & Wells cognitive model\; Morgan & R
 affle (1999)\; Salkovskis)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 13 Morning: Test your prediction
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
