SUMMARY:Day 14 Morning: Week 2 review: your Fear Map
DESCRIPTION:Week 2: The Fear Underneath. Every lie is protecting something
 .\n\nToday\, draw your Fear Map: your top three fears\, the lie each one p
 roduces\, and the truth each one avoids.\n\nBefore you go\, write today's 
 if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Lies are s
 afety behaviors. Dropping them teaches you that the truth is survivable. E
 ach lie you don't tell is a test of your prediction. The prediction test (
 Day 13) and the truth ladder (Week 5) are behavioral experiments. (Clark &
  Wells cognitive model\; Morgan & Raffle (1999)\; Salkovskis)
