 n)\n1. Lies told today (#): what\, to whom\n2. Lies caught before I spoke 
 (#)\n3. Corrections made (#)\n4. The trigger: who\, where\, how tired I wa
 s\, and the fear (failure / rejection / conflict / looking weak)\n5. The s
 tory in my head: "If I tell the truth\, ___ will happen."\n6. What actuall
 y happened when I told the truth\n7. Tomorrow's risk moment\, written as a
 n if-then: "If ___\, then I'll say ___."\n8. One line of prayer or thanks
