DTSTART:20261113T063000
DTEND:20261113T063500
SUMMARY:Day 16 Morning: Ride the urge
DESCRIPTION:Week 3: The Pause. Lies are fast. Truth needs three seconds.\n
 \nWhen the urge to lie hits today\, don't act on it right away. Rate it fr
 om 0 to 10 and watch it. Urges rise\, peak and fade\, usually within a min
 ute or two.\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, th
 en I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: A slip doesn't have to become a relapse
 . If you lie\, you correct it\, log it\, and keep going. You never go back
  to Day 1. (Marlatt & Gordon\, Relapse Prevention\; Larimer\, Palmer & Mar
 latt (1999))
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 16 Morning: Ride the urge
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
