SUMMARY:Day 17 Morning: "I don't know"
DESCRIPTION:Week 3: The Pause. Lies are fast. Truth needs three seconds.\n
 \nSay "I don't know" or "I'm not sure" at least once today instead of fill
 ing the silence with something you made up.\n\nBefore you go\, write today
 's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Lies ar
 e safety behaviors. Dropping them teaches you that the truth is survivable
 . Each lie you don't tell is a test of your prediction. The prediction tes
 t (Day 13) and the truth ladder (Week 5) are behavioral experiments. (Clar
 k & Wells cognitive model\; Morgan & Raffle (1999)\; Salkovskis)
