SUMMARY:Day 18 Morning: The 60-second correction
DESCRIPTION:Week 3: The Pause. Lies are fast. Truth needs three seconds.\n
 \nIf a lie slips out\, correct it inside a minute: "Actually\, that's not 
 true. The truth is ___." Fast correction beats a perfect record.\n\nBefore
  you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\n
 Why it works: A slip doesn't have to become a relapse. If you lie\, you co
 rrect it\, log it\, and keep going. You never go back to Day 1. (Marlatt &
  Gordon\, Relapse Prevention\; Larimer\, Palmer & Marlatt (1999))
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 18 Morning: The 60-second correction
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
