SUMMARY:Day 19 Morning: Slow down
DESCRIPTION:Week 3: The Pause. Lies are fast. Truth needs three seconds.\n
 \nIn every hard conversation today\, speak about 20% slower. Rushing feeds
  lies.\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'
 ll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: The pause interrupts an automatic response. 
 The three-second pause isn't magic. It's the gap where your prepared true 
 sentence gets a chance. (Kobis et al. (2019)\, Perspectives on Psychologic
 al Science\; Curtis & Hart (2020))
