SUMMARY:Day 23 Evening Ledger
DESCRIPTION:Tonight's question: Which true sentence still felt strange to 
 say? Say it three more times before bed.\n\nTHE LEDGER (10 min)\n1. Lies t
 old today (#): what\, to whom\n2. Lies caught before I spoke (#)\n3. Corre
 ctions made (#)\n4. The trigger: who\, where\, how tired I was\, and the f
 ear (failure / rejection / conflict / looking weak)\n5. The story in my he
 ad: "If I tell the truth\, ___ will happen."\n6. What actually happened wh
 en I told the truth\n7. Tomorrow's risk moment\, written as an if-then: "I
 f ___\, then I'll say ___."\n8. One line of prayer or thanks
