DTSTAMP:20261028T233650Z
DTSTART:20261121T063000
DTEND:20261121T063500
SUMMARY:Day 24 Morning: Say the feeling instead
DESCRIPTION:Week 4: Replace the Lie. You can't just stop. You have to say 
 something else.\n\nMany lies stand in for feelings. Today\, when the urge 
 hits\, name the feeling instead\, out loud or to yourself: "I'm embarrasse
 d." "I'm afraid I'll look bad."\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: 
 "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Writing about hard 
 things helps a little. The evening questions and letters are writing exerc
 ises. They help\, but they're one tool among several\, not a cure. (Fratta
 roli (2006)\, Psychological Bulletin)
