SUMMARY:Day 25 Morning: Private is not a lie
DESCRIPTION:Week 4: Replace the Lie. You can't just stop. You have to say 
 something else.\n\nYou're allowed to not share something. "I'd rather not 
 get into that" is honest. Making something up is not. Today\, when you wan
 t to hide something\, decline instead of inventing.\n\nBefore you go\, wri
 te today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works:
  If-then plans work. Every morning you write one if-then plan for the day'
 s risk moment: "If she asks about the money\, then I'll say the real numbe
 r." (Gollwitzer & Sheeran (2006)\, Advances in Experimental Social Psychol
 ogy)
