 , to whom\n2. Lies caught before I spoke (#)\n3. Corrections made (#)\n4. 
 The trigger: who\, where\, how tired I was\, and the fear (failure / rejec
 tion / conflict / looking weak)\n5. The story in my head: "If I tell the t
 ruth\, ___ will happen."\n6. What actually happened when I told the truth\
 n7. Tomorrow's risk moment\, written as an if-then: "If ___\, then I'll sa
