UID:truth-ledger-78@bethemansystem.com
DTSTAMP:20261028T233650Z
DTSTART:20261123T063000
DTEND:20261123T063500
SUMMARY:Day 26 Morning: No made-up excuses
DESCRIPTION:Week 4: Replace the Lie. You can't just stop. You have to say 
 something else.\n\nWhen you're late\, forget or fall short today\, state t
 he fact with no invented reason: "I'm late. I left late." "I forgot."\n\nB
 efore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___.
 "\n\nWhy it works: Lies are safety behaviors. Dropping them teaches you th
 at the truth is survivable. Each lie you don't tell is a test of your pred
 iction. The prediction test (Day 13) and the truth ladder (Week 5) are beh
 avioral experiments. (Clark & Wells cognitive model\; Morgan & Raffle (199
 9)\; Salkovskis)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 26 Morning: No made-up excuses
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
