SUMMARY:Day 27 Morning: When you're tired
DESCRIPTION:Week 4: Replace the Lie. You can't just stop. You have to say 
 something else.\n\nLook at your ledger: lies often come when you're tired\
 , rushed or stressed. Write an if-then for tonight: "If I'm worn out and s
 omeone asks me something\, then I'll say: let me answer that in the mornin
 g."\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll 
 say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Tired men have less self-control. Treat being t
 ired as a risk factor. Your evening ledger and your relapse warning signs 
 include sleep. (Barnes\, Schaubroeck\, Huth & Ghumman (2011)\, Organizatio
 nal Behavior and Human Decision Processes)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 27 Morning: When you're tired
TRIGGER:PT0M
