SUMMARY:Day 29 Morning: Build your truth ladder
DESCRIPTION:Week 5: Small Truths\, Out Loud. Courage is a muscle. Train it
  light first.\n\nList ten truths you've been avoiding\, from easiest ("I'm
  running late") to hardest. Today\, tell the easiest one.\n\nBefore you go
 \, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it 
 works: Lies are safety behaviors. Dropping them teaches you that the truth
  is survivable. Each lie you don't tell is a test of your prediction. The 
 prediction test (Day 13) and the truth ladder (Week 5) are behavioral expe
 riments. (Clark & Wells cognitive model\; Morgan & Raffle (1999)\; Salkovs
 kis)
