SUMMARY:Day 33 Morning: Take the reaction
DESCRIPTION:Week 5: Small Truths\, Out Loud. Courage is a muscle. Train it
  light first.\n\nBefore a hard truth today\, take two minutes to write abo
 ut what matters most to you: your faith\, your children\, the man you've d
 ecided to be. Then\, when the truth gets a reaction\, don't defend\, expla
 in or lie again.\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens
 \, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Remembering your values makes you 
 less defensive. Before a hard truth\, spend two minutes writing about what
  matters most to you: your faith\, your children\, the man you've decided 
 to be (Day 33). (Sherman & Cohen (2002)\, Current Directions in Psychologi
 cal Science)
