DTSTART:20261201T063000
DTEND:20261201T063500
SUMMARY:Day 34 Morning: Climb again
DESCRIPTION:Week 5: Small Truths\, Out Loud. Courage is a muscle. Train it
  light first.\n\nTell rung five or six of your ladder today.\n\nBefore you
  go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy 
 it works: Lies are safety behaviors. Dropping them teaches you that the tr
 uth is survivable. Each lie you don't tell is a test of your prediction. T
 he prediction test (Day 13) and the truth ladder (Week 5) are behavioral e
 xperiments. (Clark & Wells cognitive model\; Morgan & Raffle (1999)\; Salk
 ovskis)
