SUMMARY:Day 37 Morning: Work
DESCRIPTION:Week 6: Hard Truths. Tell the truth where it costs the most.\n
 \nAt work today\, no inflating your progress and no excuses for what isn't
  done. Report exactly where things stand.\n\nBefore you go\, write today's
  if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Trying to
  look competent or likable makes people lie more. Your two fears\, failing
  and not being accepted\, are exactly these two goals. Week 2 teaches you 
 to notice which one is running in the moment. (Feldman\, Forrest & Happ (2
 002)\, Basic and Applied Social Psychology)
