SUMMARY:Day 38 Morning: Answer the whole question
DESCRIPTION:Week 6: Hard Truths. Tell the truth where it costs the most.\n
 \nWhen someone asks you something today\, especially at home\, answer it f
 ully the first time. A half-answer is a lie with better manners.\n\nBefore
  you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\n
 Why it works: Trust after lying comes back slowly\, through actions. Set y
 our expectations: people believe you again slowly\, and words won't carry 
 you. Answer fully the first time (Day 38) and keep small\, specific promis
 es exactly (Day 41). (Schweitzer\, Hershey & Bradlow (2006)\, Organization
 al Behavior and Human Decision Processes)
