DTSTART:20261207T063000
DTEND:20261207T063500
SUMMARY:Day 40 Morning: No covering lies
DESCRIPTION:Week 6: Hard Truths. Tell the truth where it costs the most.\n
 \nWhen an old lie comes up today\, don't tell a new lie to protect it. If 
 you're not ready to correct it\, say nothing. Never add another layer.\n\n
 Before you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___
 ."\n\nWhy it works: Small lies make bigger lies easier. There's no such th
 ing as a harmless small lie for you. Every exaggeration trains the slope. 
 That's why Day 20 is "No rounding up." (Garrett\, Lazzaro\, Ariely & Sharo
 t (2016)\, Nature Neuroscience)
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 40 Morning: No covering lies
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
