SUMMARY:Day 43 Morning: Your identity sentence
DESCRIPTION:Week 7: A Man Whose Word Holds. Not a streak. An identity.\n\n
 Rewrite your vision sentence: "I am a man who tells the truth when it cost
 s me." Read it three times this morning.\n\nBefore you go\, write today's 
 if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: Rememberin
 g your values makes you less defensive. Before a hard truth\, spend two mi
 nutes writing about what matters most to you: your faith\, your children\,
  the man you've decided to be (Day 33). (Sherman & Cohen (2002)\, Current 
 Directions in Psychological Science)
