SUMMARY:Day 44 Morning: Your warning signs
DESCRIPTION:Week 7: A Man Whose Word Holds. Not a streak. An identity.\n\n
 Write your relapse warning signs: short on sleep\, stressed\, money troubl
 e\, skipping the ledger\, keeping "small" secrets\, rounding up again.\n\n
 Before you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___
 ."\n\nWhy it works: Tired men have less self-control. Treat being tired as
  a risk factor. Your evening ledger and your relapse warning signs include
  sleep. (Barnes\, Schaubroeck\, Huth & Ghumman (2011)\, Organizational Beh
 avior and Human Decision Processes)
