DTEND:20261212T063500
SUMMARY:Day 45 Morning: Your relapse plan
DESCRIPTION:Week 7: A Man Whose Word Holds. Not a streak. An identity.\n\n
 Write it and sign it: If I lie\, I will 1) correct it the same day\, 2) lo
 g it honestly\, 3) write myself two honest\, kind sentences instead of tea
 ring myself down\, 4) reread my if-then plans\, 5) keep going. I don't sta
 rt over at Day 1.\n\nBefore you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happen
 s\, then I'll say ___."\n\nWhy it works: A slip doesn't have to become a r
 elapse. If you lie\, you correct it\, log it\, and keep going. You never g
 o back to Day 1. (Marlatt & Gordon\, Relapse Prevention\; Larimer\, Palmer
  & Marlatt (1999))
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Day 45 Morning: Your relapse plan
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
