SUMMARY:Day 47 Morning: What the truth gave you
DESCRIPTION:Week 7: A Man Whose Word Holds. Not a streak. An identity.\n\n
 List five things that seven weeks of telling the truth have given you.\n\n
 Before you go\, write today's if-then: "If ___ happens\, then I'll say ___
 ."\n\nWhy it works: Self-compassion makes men more likely to make amends. 
 Beating yourself up feeds shame\, and shame feeds hiding. After a slip\, y
 ou write yourself two honest\, kind sentences\, then you go fix it. (Brein
 es & Chen (2012)\, Personality and Social Psychology Bulletin)
